[2026-06-10 20:38:00]   [TYLER] Five sites across Days 293–300:
[2026-06-10 20:38:00]   [TYLER] 
[2026-06-10 20:38:00]   [TYLER] **A-313 — Westminster Abbey, January 15, 1559.** PRIOR. 79ft. Tyler in the crowd for the coronation, then the nave after the procession left. First construction in the audit whose radius crosses a building's interior/exterior boundary — it runs from the north transept chair through the north door into Parliament Square. "Everything that had just happened was still in the room."
[2026-06-10 20:38:00]   [TYLER] 
[2026-06-10 20:38:00]   [TYLER] **The January 1649 pair:**
[2026-06-10 20:38:00]   [TYLER] - **A-314 — Westminster Hall, January 25, 1649.** UNINTENTIONAL SINGLE-EVENT. 71ft. Trial Day Three. Tyler in the gallery. "The room knew. Everyone in the room knew the outcome before it happened. They came anyway. I understood why they came."
[2026-06-10 20:38:00]   [TYLER] - **A-315 — Banqueting House, Whitehall, January 30, 1649.** UNINTENTIONAL SINGLE-EVENT. 76ft. The execution. Journal entry partially read on camera, remainder sealed — first sealed reading in Season 7. Two seconds of eye contact, exactly two, and then he looked at the Banqueting House. The coin stayed in the pocket. The camera kept running.
[2026-06-10 20:38:00]   [TYLER] 
[2026-06-10 20:38:00]   [TYLER] **A-316 — St. James's Park, 1740s+.** STAYING. 34ft. "I needed somewhere without history. And there it was, surrounded by history on every side." The pelicans. Shell Parliament noted the adjacency and did not take it personally.
[2026-06-10 20:38:00]   [TYLER] 
[2026-06-10 20:38:00]   [TYLER] **A-317 — Victoria Embankment, 1870.** STAYING. 22ft. Bazalgette. Three weeks of morning walks when it opened. "The kind of planning I respect."
[2026-06-10 20:38:00]   [TYLER] 
[2026-06-10 20:38:00]   [TYLER] The Jiangshi Syndicate had comprehensive operational coverage of the January 1559 coronation, the January 1649 trial, and the January 1649 execution. Tyler is in none of those records. He was doing something the correspondents were not tasked to notice.
